

1. Introductory Clause
OUTPUT:

This Agreement is made and entered into as of January 1, 2023, by and between Golden Bank, a leading financial institution based in New York City, acting as Lender, and Tech Innovations Inc., a technology company headquartered in Silicon Valley, acting as Borrower.

The Lender hereby agrees to lend to the Borrower the sum of ten million dollars ($10,000,000) for the purpose of expanding the Borrower's research and development department. The Borrower acknowledges and agrees to repay the loan in equal monthly installments over a period of five years, with an annual interest rate of 5%.

In consideration of the mutual covenants, promises, and conditions contained herein, the parties hereto agree as follows.

2. Parties
Golden Bank, a leading financial institution based in New York City, acting as Lender, and Tech Innovations Inc., a technology company headquartered in Silicon Valley, acting as Borrower, hereby agree to the terms and conditions set forth in this Agreement.

Golden Bank, the Lender, is located at Golden Bank, 123 Main Street, New York, NY 10001, USA, and can be contacted at (123) 456-7890 or info@goldenbank.com.

Tech Innovations Inc., the Borrower, is located at Tech Innovations Inc., 456 Elm Street, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA, and can be contacted at (987) 654-3210 or info@techinnovations.com.

3. Loan Terms
The Lender agrees to lend the sum of ten million dollars ($10,000,000) to the Borrower. The Borrower acknowledges and agrees to repay the loan in equal monthly installments over a period of five years, commencing on January 1, 2024. The annual interest rate on the loan shall be 5%. The Borrower shall make all payments on or before the due date each month.

In the event of any default by the Borrower, the Lender may exercise any and all remedies available to it under applicable law, including, but not limited to, the seizure of the Borrower's assets to recover the outstanding loan amount.

4. Definitions
(a) "Agreement" means this Loan Agreement, dated as of January 1, 2023, between Golden Bank and Tech Innovations Inc.

(b) "Borrower" means Tech Innovations Inc., a technology company headquartered in Silicon Valley, acting as the borrower of the loan.

(c) "Lender" means Golden Bank, a leading financial institution based in New York City, acting as the lender of the loan.

(d) "Loan Amount" means the sum of ten million dollars ($10,000,000) lent by the Lender to the Borrower.

(e) "Interest Rate" means an annual interest rate of 5%.

(f) "Repayment Terms" means equal monthly installments over a period of five years, commencing on January 1, 2024.

(g) "Default" means any failure by the Borrower to make any payment when due or to perform any other obligation under this Agreement.

(h) "Governing Law" means the laws of the state of New York.

(i) "Assets" means any and all property, real or personal, tangible or intangible, owned by the Borrower, which may be seized by the Lender in the event of default.

(j) "Witnesses" means Jane Doe and John Smith, who can be contacted at jane.doe@goldenbank.com and john.smith@goldenbank.com, respectively.

5. Representations and Warranties
The Lender and the Borrower hereby represent and warrant as follows:

(a) Authority: Each party has the full power and authority to execute and deliver this Agreement and to perform its obligations hereunder.

(b) Loan Purpose: The Borrower will use the Loan Amount solely for the purpose of expanding its research and development department.

(c) Repayment Ability: The Borrower has the financial ability to make all payments required under this Agreement when due, and the Loan Amount, when combined with the Borrower's other obligations, will not exceed the Borrower's ability to repay.

(d) No Conflicts: There are no legal or other impediments preventing the execution, delivery, or performance of this Agreement.

(e) Accuracy: All information provided by the Borrower to the Lender in connection with this Agreement is true, complete, and accurate in all material respects.

(f) No Default: As of the date hereof, the Borrower is not in default under any material agreement to which it is a party or by which it is bound.

(g) Governing Law: This Agreement is governed by the laws of the state of New York.

(h) Entire Agreement: This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the parties regarding the subject matter hereof, and supersedes all prior negotiations, understandings, and agreements between the parties.

(i) Amendments: This Agreement may be amended or modified only in writing signed by both parties.

(j) Counterparts: This Agreement may be executed in counterparts, each of which shall be deemed an original, but all of which together shall constitute one and the same instrument.

(k) Binding Effect: This Agreement shall be binding upon and inure to the benefit of the parties and their respective successors and assigns.

(l) Notices: All notices, requests, demands, and other communications under this Agreement shall be in writing and shall be deemed duly given when delivered in person or sent by registered or certified mail, postage prepaid, or by email to the respective addresses set forth in the preamble or to such other address as either party may designate by written notice to the other party.

(m) Waiver: No waiver by either party of any default, misrepresentation, or breach of warranty or covenant hereunder, whether intentional or not, shall be deemed to extend to any prior or subsequent default, misrepresentation, or breach of warranty or covenant hereunder or affect in any way any rights arising by virtue of any prior or subsequent such occurrence.

(n) Severability: If any provision of this Agreement is held to be invalid, illegal, or unenforceable in any respect under any applicable law or rule in any jurisdiction, such invalidity, illegality, or unenforceability shall not affect any other provisions of this Agreement or invalidate or render unenforceable such provision in any other jurisdiction.

(o) Headings: The headings in this Agreement are for convenience only and shall not affect the construction or interpretation of this Agreement.

6. Interest and Fees
SECTION 6:
The Borrower shall pay interest on the outstanding principal balance of the Loan at an annual rate of five percent (5%). The interest shall be calculated on the basis of a 360-day year (ACT/ACT) and shall be payable in equal monthly installments concurrently with the principal repayments. The Borrower shall also be responsible for any fees and charges incurred in connection with the Loan, including but not limited to, document preparation fees, wire transfer fees, and any other fees or charges as may be agreed upon by the parties in writing.

7. Default and Remedies
(a) Default: The Borrower shall be deemed to be in default if it fails to make any payment when due or breaches any of its representations, warranties, or covenants under this Agreement.

(b) Remedies: In the event of default, the Lender may, without prejudice to any other rights or remedies it may have, exercise any of the following remedies:

(i) Acceleration: The Lender may declare all amounts outstanding under this Agreement immediately due and payable.

(ii) Setoff: The Lender may set off any amounts owed by the Borrower to the Lender against any amounts due from the Lender to the Borrower.

(iii) Assignment: The Lender may assign its rights and delegate its obligations under this Agreement to any third party.

(iv) Foreclosure: The Lender may foreclose on any collateral securing the Loan and sell the same at public or private sale, with or without notice, for cash or credit, and upon such terms and conditions as the Lender deems appropriate.

(v) Injunction: The Lender may apply to any court of competent jurisdiction for an injunction or other equitable relief to prevent any breach or continuation of a breach by the Borrower of any of its obligations under this Agreement.

(c) Notice: Any exercise by the Lender of its remedies under this Section shall be subject to the Lender providing the Borrower with written notice of the default and the intention to exercise such remedies, unless such notice is waived by the Borrower in writing.

(d) Cure: The Borrower shall have the right to cure any default within ten (10) business days of receiving notice of such default from the Lender, provided that the Borrower promptly remedies the default and continues to perform its obligations under this Agreement in all respects.

(e) Damages: In the event of any default by the Borrower, the Lender shall be entitled to recover from the Borrower any damages it sustains as a result of such default, in addition to any other remedies available to the Lender under this Agreement or at law.

8. Security
SECTION:

(a) Collateral: As security for the Loan, the Borrower hereby grants to the Lender a first priority lien on all of its assets, including, but not limited to, its accounts receivable, inventory, equipment, intellectual property, and real property, located anywhere in the world.

(b) Additional Security: The Borrower agrees to execute such additional documents and take such further actions as the Lender may reasonably request to perfect, maintain, and enforce its security interest in the collateral.

(c) Change of Control: In the event of a change of control of the Borrower, the Borrower shall provide the Lender with written notice of such change of control and shall cooperate with the Lender to ensure that the Lender's security interest in the collateral is preserved.

(d) Non-Exclusivity: The grant of security in this Section is in addition to, and not in lieu of, any other security that the Lender may take in connection with the Loan.

(e) Perfection: The Lender shall perfect its security interest in the collateral by filing financing statements in the appropriate jurisdictions and taking such other actions as may be required by applicable law.

(f) Priority: The Lender's security interest in the collateral shall have priority over the rights of any other creditors of the Borrower, except for any security interests that have priority by operation of law.

(g) Application of Payments: Any payments made by the Borrower shall be applied first to any fees, expenses, and charges incurred by the Lender, then to any accrued and unpaid interest, and finally to the principal amount of the Loan, in each case in such order as the Lender may determine.

(h) Rights of Setoff: The Lender shall have the right to set off any amounts owed by the Borrower to the Lender against any amounts due from the Lender to the Borrower.

(i) Assignment: The Lender may assign its rights and delegate its obligations under this Agreement to any third party, provided that such assignee agrees to assume the Lender's obligations with respect to the collateral.

(j) Foreclosure: The Lender may foreclose on any collateral securing the Loan and sell the same at public or private sale, with or without notice, for cash or credit, and upon such terms and conditions as the Lender deems appropriate.

(k) Injunction: The Lender may apply to any court of competent jurisdiction for an injunction or other equitable relief to prevent any breach or continuation of a breach by the Borrower of any of its obligations under this Agreement.

(l) Notice: Any exercise by the Lender of its remedies under this Section shall be subject to the Lender providing the Borrower with written notice of the default and the intention to exercise such remedies, unless such notice is waived by the Borrower in writing.

(m) Cure: The Borrower shall have the right to cure any default within ten (10) business days of receiving notice of such default from the Lender, provided that the Borrower promptly remedies the default and continues to perform its obligations under this Agreement in all respects.

(n) Damages: In the event of any default by the Borrower, the Lender shall be entitled to recover from the Borrower any damages it sustains as a result of such default, in addition to any other remedies available to the Lender under this Agreement or at law.

9. Governing Law
SECTION 9:
This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of New York, without giving effect to its conflict of laws principles. Any action or proceeding arising out of or relating to this Agreement shall be brought exclusively in the federal or state courts located in the City of New York, County of New York, and the parties hereby irrevocably submit to the jurisdiction of such courts.

The Borrower hereby waives any objection it may now or hereafter have to the laying of venue of any such action or proceeding brought in such courts, and any claim that any such action or proceeding brought in such courts has been brought in an inconvenient forum.

The Borrower further agrees that service of process in any such action or proceeding may be effected by mailing a copy thereof to the Borrower at its address set forth in Section 2 of this Agreement.

The Lender shall be entitled to recover from the Borrower all costs and expenses, including reasonable attorneys' fees, incurred in enforcing any right of the Lender arising out of or relating to this Agreement, including in connection with any action or proceeding brought to foreclose any mortgage or security interest granted by the Borrower to the Lender.

